# The limit that "./setup.sh queue" adds to lsb.resources (shown here for reference; one row per
# host of bench.conf, with the host name LSF uses and the cores lshosts reports).
# Vertical tabular Limit section, IBM Spectrum LSF 10.1.0 printed pp. 1695-1696; NAME at most 40
# characters (p. 1701). Queue build may use at most SLOTS job slots on that host. PJOB_LIMIT and
# SLOTS_PER_PROCESSOR are not used: with PARALLEL_SCHED_BY_SLOT=Y (set by the installer) LSF counts
# each job slot as a processor, so they scale with MXJ instead of the cores.
# Author: P M Shabbir Hussain

# >>> lsf-build-bench limit build (added by setup.sh; remove with: setup.sh remove)
# queue build: at most one job slot per core on each server (cores = lshosts ncpus)
Begin Limit
NAME                                     QUEUES       HOSTS                                SLOTS
bf_build_1_hostA                         build        hostA                                16
bf_build_2_hostB                         build        hostB                                2
bf_build_3_hostC                         build        hostC                                16
End Limit
# <<< lsf-build-bench limit build
